virtual dom?
React creates a virtual DOM — it's just a copy of the real DOM in memory.
When the data (state/props) changes, React:Updates the virtual DOM first
Compares the new virtual DOM with the old one (called "diffing")
React then updates only the changed parts in the real DOM — not the whole page.
